STRUCTURES

Structures help define a list of qualities to be kept-note of in a single variable, basically a big variable that has smaller compartments one can store set information in.
Its syntax is as follows:

public struct name-of-structure
{
  public data-type variable-name
  ...
}

EX:
  public struct ComponentsOfHotdog
  {
    public string BunType;
    public string MeatType;
    public string GarnishOrToppings;
  }

//invoked, this would be:

ComponentsOfHotdog D423;
D423.BunType = "Extra-Long Hotdog Bun.";
D423.MeatType = "Sausage with chilli.";
D423.GarnishOrToppings = "Green Onion.";

// this binds said answeres to each corresponding variable under the name alloted.

Beware! You should not confuse Structures with Class, they server different purpouses and are not interexchangeable terms! One refers to Value types (struct) and the other to Reference types (class).

